+{
+  "task_id": "advanced/execution-lifecycle/transfer",
+  "repository": "earendil-works/pi",
+  "mode": "repair",
+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Ran from the workspace root with Node (stripTypeScriptTypes/VM modules): all assertions passed. Three one-line repairs: drive/tools.ts persists only options.checkpoint === true progress while still emitting every admitted update via lane.emitBatch; execution/tools.ts classifies a thrown tool as isError: true so the published ToolResultMessage stays an error; effect-gate.ts signalAbort() aborts the gate-owned AbortController so the already-admitted tool's AbortSignal fires while beginAbort keeps refusing new admissions with AbortRequested. The regression covers recovered safe replay with checkpointed plus live-only updates followed by a tool throw (checkpoints persisted exactly, updates observed in order, final isError true, drain before publish), a promise-held drain showing publication is withheld until progress drain completes, abort delivered to the running tool's signal, direct gate admission/close semantics, and the non-replayed interrupted recovery path. Per-file baseline verification: restoring drive/tools.ts, execution/tools.ts, or effect-gate.ts alone to its faulty baseline makes the same script fail with a genuine node:assert/strict AssertionError (no crash, import error or timeout). No timers, randomness, network, dependencies or external services are used; the subject helper is fully in-memory, so no temporary fixtures remain."
+  }
+}
